assessment#:#send_simple_results_to_participants_confirm#:#Send result in an e-mail to selected candidates?<br />The name, student registration number, date of the test run and the text feedback are included in the email for the evaluated test run.
assessment#:#send_simple_results_to_participants_failed#:#It was not possible to send a message to the following users:<br />%s
assessment#:#send_simple_results_to_participants_success#:#A message was sent to the following users:<br />%s
assessment#:#sent_simple_results_to_participants#:#The results were sent to the participants.
assessment#:#show_detailed_results_with_correct_solutions#:#Detailed examination results with correct solutions (evaluated test run)
assessment#:#tst_authorship_statement#:#Declaration of originality
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_by#:#Order of the questions
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_by_info#:#If the test does not generally mix the questions, the questions of this selection rule remain in consecutive order. You can choose how to sort them here.
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_description#:#According to description
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_random#:#Randomly
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_title#:#According to title
assessment#:#tst_filter_order_undefined#:#Unsorted
assessment#:#tst_group_filter#:#Group selection
assessment#:#tst_group_filter_info#:#All questions should belong to the same taxonomy node
assessment#:#tst_group_filter_info_warning#:#Warning: A group selection rule can put stricter limits on the questions available than during the check carried out to see whether enough questions are available that are not required for other rules. This means that the group selection function may only be used in rules that do not overlap with other rules.
assessment#:#tst_group_filter_tax#:#Group taxonomy
assessment#:#tst_group_filter_tax_info#:#The taxonomy must be activated as a filter. One of the nodes is selected at random from your selected nodes and the questions are extracted from the node. Only nodes that contain enough questions are used.
assessment#:#tst_info_section_requirements#:#Prerequisite for starting the test
assessment#:#tst_mark_tst_failed#:#Resulting grade fail
assessment#:#tst_mark_tst_failed_details#:#This text replaces the standard message on the results page of a failed test. You can use the following placeholders in the message:<br /><strong>[mark]</strong> : official designation of the grade,<br /><strong>[markshort]</strong> : short designation of the grade,<br /><strong>[percentage]</strong> : percentage solved,<br /><strong>[reached]</strong> : points achieved,<br /><strong>[max]</strong> : maximum number of points.
assessment#:#tst_mark_tst_passed#:#Resulting grade pass
assessment#:#tst_mark_tst_passed_details#:#This text replaces the standard message on the results page of a passed test. You can use the following placeholders in the message:<br /><strong>[mark]</strong> : official designation of the grade,<br /><strong>[markshort]</strong> : short designation of the grade,<br /><strong>[percentage]</strong> : percentage solved,<br /><strong>[reached]</strong> : points achieved,<br /><strong>[max]</strong> : maximum number of points.
assessment#:#tst_msg_authorship_statement_required#:#Please read and confirm the declaration of originality.
assessment#:#tst_msg_rand_quest_set_has_double_originals#:#The random set of questions contains duplicate originals. Please synchronize the test again, preferably not via a load balancer.
assessment#:#tst_msg_rand_quest_set_pass_not_buildable_detail#:#There are fewer than the required questions for rule %s. For each rule, there must be enough questions that do not match any other rules.
assessment#:#tst_msg_rand_quest_set_pass_not_buildable_group#:#No question group was found with the required number of questions for the %s rule.
assessment#:#tst_msg_rand_quest_set_pool_not_available#:#The selected question pool is not available. It is either offline, not readable or contains questions with varying numbers of points.
assessment#:#tst_msg_rand_quest_set_sync_duration#:#All questions that match the rules are copied into the test during synchronization. This action can take several minutes for large pools.
assessment#:#tst_password_enter_info#:#IMPORTANT: Please do not change the password while a written examination is taking place. The participants must enter it when changing questions in order to continue. Previous auto saves will fail.
assessment#:#tst_question_browse_root_message#:#A search is performed as standard in the category or folder that contains this test. This can be changed with the filter settings.
assessment#:#tst_recalculate_selected_solutions_confirm#:#The results of the selected participants will be recalculated. Manual evaluations remain intact.
assessment#:#tst_recalculate_solutions#:#Recalculate results
assessment#:#tst_recalculate_solutions_confirm#:#The results of all participants will be recalculated. Manual evaluations remain intact. This calculation may take a long time.
assessment#:#tst_recalculated_solutions#:#The results have been recalculated.
assessment#:#tst_require_authorship_statement#:#Declaration of originality
assessment#:#tst_require_authorship_statement_desc#:#Requires confirmation of a declaration of originality before the test can begin
assessment#:#tst_tbl_col_pass_finished#:#Last evaluated access
assessment#:#tst_tbl_col_started_passes#:#Runs started
assessment#:#tst_use_previous_answer#:#Confirm the displayed solutions from the previous run
assessment#:#tst_use_previous_answer_imagemap#:#Please click on the image again to confirm the solution from the previous run.
assessment#:#tst_use_previous_answers_authorized#:#Copy the previous solutions into the new test run. They have already been saved, but can still be changed.
assessment#:#validate_submit_error#:#Your entry has not been saved.
assessment#:#validate_submit_error_in_test_hint#:#You can only exit the question after you have corrected your entry. Alternatively, you can undo your changes.
assessment#:#warning_delete_scored_pass#:#ATTENTION: This is the evaluated test run. It should only be deleted in the case of an error.
auth#:#shib_continue#:#Continue to StudOn
auth#:#shib_continue_local#:#Continue to StudOn
auth#:#shib_convert_accept#:#I accept the changes.
auth#:#shib_convert_cancel#:#Continue without changing
auth#:#shib_convert_change_login#:#Your <strong>StudOn user name</strong> <em>%s</em> will be changed to <em>%s</em>. It will be used in forums, member lists and for messages within StudOn in future.
auth#:#shib_convert_denied#:#You must be logged on via single sign-on in order to carry out the change.
auth#:#shib_convert_head#:#Changeover to single sign-on
auth#:#shib_convert_intro#:#<p>Dear user,</p><p>you have just successfully logged on via <a href="http://www.studon.uni-erlangen.de/cat166816.html">single sign-on</a>. You can now change your StudOn log in to standard. This involves the following <strong>changes</strong>:</p>
auth#:#shib_convert_keep_login#:#Your <strong>StudOn user name</strong> <em>%s</em> will remain the same. However, to log in via single sign-on, please use <em>%s</em>.
auth#:#shib_convert_name#:#Your <strong>first name</strong> and <strong>last name</strong> will be updated automatically and you are no longer able to change it in StudOn.
auth#:#shib_convert_not_accepted#:#Please agree to the changes.
auth#:#shib_convert_outro#:#<p>During the changeover, you must accept the user agreement of StudOn again.</p>
auth#:#shib_convert_password#:#Your <strong>password</strong> will be updated automatically and you are no longer able to change it in StudOn. You can change your password in <a target="_blank" href="https://www.idm.uni-erlangen.de">identity management self service</a><span class="ilAccHidden"> (new window)</span>.
auth#:#shib_convert_submit#:#Carry out changeover
auth#:#shib_inactive_head#:#Inactive account
auth#:#shib_inactive_text#:#<p>If you are studying at Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), you can log in via <a href="http://www.studon.uni-erlangen.de/cat166816.html">single sign-on</a> to activate your StudOn user account. Please use your user ID and password for the central login service that you can change in the <a target="_blank" href="https://www.idm.uni-erlangen.de">identity management self service</a><span class="ilAccHidden"> (new window)</span>. Your central user ID is also your StudOn username.</p><p>If you are not studying at Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU), please send a message to <a href="mailto:studon@fau.de">studon@fau.de</a>.</p>
auth#:#shib_not_creatable_head#:#Single sign-on without a student registration number
auth#:#shib_not_creatable_text#:#<p>Dear user,</p><p>We were unable to find the correct StudOn user for your personal university account. A new StudOn account can currently only be generated automatically for students whose student registration number is submitted during single sign-on.</p><p>If you <strong>already have a StudOn login</strong>, please send it to us together with your personal university account via e-mail to the following address: <a href="mailto:studon@fau.de">studon@fau.de</a>. This will enable us to match both to each other, so that you are able to use single sign-on.</p><p>If you are enrolled as a <strong>student</strong> at the University for the current semester and have paid your semester fee, your student registration number should have already been submitted. Please contact <a href="mailto:sso-support@uni-erlangen.de">SSO support</a> at the RRZE helpdesk to solve the problem.</p><p>If you are an FAU <strong>employee</strong>, please use the <a href="http://www.studon.uni-erlangen.de/info/registrierung.html">registration form for employees</a>. Please enter your personal university user account in this case also.
auth#:#shib_recommendation_head#:#Changeover to single sign-on
auth#:#shib_recommendation_text#:#<p>Dear user,<br /></p><p>In StudOn, <a href="http://www.studon.uni-erlangen.de/cat166816.html">single sign-on</a> is the preferred method of logging in for students and is also recommended for teaching staff.</p><p class="alert">Only single sign-on updates your user data, which can affect your ability to join courses and groups.</p><p>You can log in using single sign-on now and set your StudOn account to use single sign-on as the standard log-in method. Please use your personal FAU user account ID and password that you can change in the <a target="_blank" href="https://www.idm.uni-erlangen.de">identity management self service</a><span class="ilAccHidden"> (new window)</span>.
auth#:#shib_reminder_head#:#Please use single sign-on
auth#:#shib_reminder_text#:#<p>Dear user,</p><p> <a href="http://www.studon.uni-erlangen.de/cat166816.html">single sign-on</a> has been set as standard via the Universitys central login service for your StudOn user account. Please use this as your preferred login method.</p><p class="alert">Only single sign-on updates your user data, which can affect your ability to join courses and groups.</p><p>You can use the local login if single sign-on is not working.</p>
auth#:#shib_to_sso#:#Single sign-on
awrn#:#awrn_hide_from_awareness_info#:#The Who is online function in the notifications section at the top of the application shows whether selected users are online (e.g. contacts from your courses and groups, lecturers). Only networked contacts from your own list of contacts (confirmed contacts) or any contact requests you have sent are displayed. Users who do not wish to show their online status are not displayed. Course administrators can display themselves as lecturers in the WIO (who is online) section if Tutor support is activated in the Members tab.
awrn#:#legal_visibility#:#<p>Here you can decide about your visibility in your courses and groups and define whether your user name is displayed in the Who is online status and whether you can be sent contact requests or receive chat messages from other course and group members. </p> <br/> <p style="color: red;">The functions have been designed as opt-ins, which means they are deactivated in the default settings of a users personal profile. Users are free to decide which individual functions they wish to activate and can only activate them after giving their express permission. The Data protection checklist shows what elements of your personal profile are visible to other users. </p>
book#:#book_user_storno#:#Enable cancellations
book#:#book_user_storno_info#:#Users should be able to cancel their own bookings. If not, only users with write permission can do so.
buddysystem#:#buddy_allow_to_contact_me_info#:#If the feature is activated, other users from my courses or groups can send me contact requests. Contact requests sent to the members of ones own courses and groups can either be sent, deactivated or withdrawn via the Members tab in courses/groups or in the main menu via Communication > Contacts. Only members who have activated the Allow contact requests function can be contacted. New contact requests are displayed with the bell symbol in notifications and can be confirmed or ignored.
chatroom#:#chat_osc_accept_msg_info#:#If activated, other users can send me messages via the on-screen chat. A conversation with another user from your contact list can be started via the notifications section via the Who is online list. Chats are only permitted with users from your courses and groups or with confirmed contacts who have activated the Chats permitted function.
cntr#:#cntr_container_only_on_their_own#:#Categories, courses, groups and folders can only be copied individually. Please select only one at a time.
common#:#accept_updated_user_agreement#:#The user agreement has been revised. No changes have been made to the number of features of the system. Please accept the user agreement at the end of this page in order to continue using the system.
common#:#accept_user_agreement#:#Please accept the user agreement at the end of this page to use the system.
