common#:#role_unbreak_permissions_desc#:#All local permissions for this role have been deleted. All permission settings can therefore be forced for all objects using the commands change existing objects and protect rights.
common#:#rpl_info#:#If possible, please choose a starting point when no other registrations are due to start.
common#:#rpl_next_week#:#Following week
common#:#rpl_overview#:#Overview of starting dates for registration
common#:#rpl_overview_desc#:#This table shows the dates on which registration is planned to start for groups and courses with restrictions on participant numbers. The number of places for which registration is starting are added up for each time period. High values indicate high numbers of people accessing the system, however, other factors also come into play, for example the popularity of courses. Please choose a free time slot for opening registration to your courses if possible. A high system load is generally to be expected in the first two weeks of the lecture period.
common#:#rpl_previous_week#:#Previous week
common#:#rpl_warning#:#Registration starts at the same time as other courses with a total exceeding %s places. A higher system load is therefore to be expected. If possible, please choose another time.
common#:#saml_log_in#:#Login###fau: loginForm
common#:#saml_login_form_info_txt#:#As a member of FAU, you can log in to StudOn with your IdM-ID » <strong><a href="https://www.studon.fau.de/studon/goto.php?target=cat_166816">Help</a></strong>###fau: loginForm
common#:#saml_login_form_txt#:#Login with Single Sign-On###fau: loginForm
common#:#score#:#Points
common#:#select_all_page_only#:#Select all on this page. Allow more lines to be shown per page in order to be able to select all.
common#:#shib_data_missing#:#Your single sign-on was successful, but data are missing (first name or last name). Without this data we cannot set up a user account in StudOn. Please contact IDM support <a href="mailto:idm@fau.de">idm@fau.de</a> in order to solve the problem, stating your user ID and the missing data.
common#:#shib_help_title#:#Help with single sign-on
common#:#shib_login_used#:#The user name %s is already being used by another user. Please contact <a href="mailto:studon@fau.de">studon@fau.de</a> to solve the problem.
common#:#shib_updated_field#:#This box is filled automatically during single sign-on.
common#:#shib_user_not_found#:#No user account was found in this installation for your user ID. Automatic creation is not possible.
common#:#start#:#Start
common#:#studon_login_exportrequest#:#Please log in to request export.
common#:#studon_ref_id#:#StudOn ID
common#:#sub_added_member#:#A new member has been accepted.
common#:#sub_added_members#:#%s new members have been accepted.
common#:#sub_added_to_waiting_list#:#You have been placed on the waiting list. <br />You are number %s on the waiting list.
common#:#sub_assign_waiting#:#Accept directly
common#:#sub_assign_waiting_fair_info#:#If you accept individual members directly from the waiting list you avoid ensuring that all earlier applicants have equal chances of receiving a place and you circumvent the principle of first come first served for those who register later. You should only do this under exceptional circumstances.
common#:#sub_assign_waiting_groupings_info#:#You have established a restriction on membership. When accepted, the applications will also be removed from the waiting lists of linked courses/groups.
common#:#sub_confirm_request#:#Accept application
common#:#sub_confirm_request_question#:#Are you sure that you would like to accept the following applications for admission? The accepted applications will remain on the list until it is their turn to fill vacancies.
common#:#sub_confirm_requests#:#Accept applications
common#:#sub_confirmed_request#:#An application for admission has been accepted.
common#:#sub_confirmed_requests#:#%s applications for admission have been accepted.
common#:#sub_fair_activate#:#Activate the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place.
common#:#sub_fair_activated#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been activated.
common#:#sub_fair_activation_min_minutes#:#The limited availability period must last at least %s minutes.
common#:#sub_fair_added_to_waiting_list#:#You have been placed on the waiting list and will receive e-mail notification after the end of the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place informing you whether you have been allocated a place or whether you are still on the waiting list.
common#:#sub_fair_auto_manu#:#Automatic allocation of places/manual assignment of places on waiting list
common#:#sub_fair_auto_manu_info#:#Places are allocated automatically once the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place finishes. Places that subsequently become free have to be filled manually using the participant management function.
common#:#sub_fair_autofill#:#Automatic allocation of places and assignment of places on waiting list
common#:#sub_fair_autofill_info#:#Places are allocated automatically after the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place. Pending applications automatically move up to fill the spaces that have become free. If free places are required for pending applications for admission, the lecturers receive a message and the places are kept free.
common#:#sub_fair_date#:#Phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place lasts until
common#:#sub_fair_date_default#:#one hour after the start of registration (standard)
common#:#sub_fair_date_info#:#Until this point, all applications are assigned to the waiting list with equal chances of receiving a place, and the free places are then drawn by lot after this point. All following applications receive a higher place on the waiting list. Applications received during the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place are also drawn by lot when moving up from the waiting list.
common#:#sub_fair_date_invalid#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place must last at least one hour and must be finished at the latest by the end of the registration period.
common#:#sub_fair_deactivate#:#Deactivate phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place
common#:#sub_fair_deactivate_explanation#:#NB: You should only deactivate the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place if you do not expect there to be a run on registration. As a rule, students assume that they have one hour after the registration period begins to register without this having a negative effect on their chances of gaining a place. Choosing to allocate places on a first come, first served basis instead goes against this solution that was agreed in close consultation with students representatives.
common#:#sub_fair_deactivate_in_phase#:#You cannot deactivate the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place, as it is currently underway.
common#:#sub_fair_deactivate_question#:#Would you like to deactivate the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place?
common#:#sub_fair_deactivated#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been deactivated.
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_autofill#:#Automatic assignment of places on the waiting list
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_autofill_info#:#Pending applications automatically move up to fill the spaces that have become free. If free places are required for pending applications for admission, the lecturers receive a message and the places are kept free.
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_message#:#For this course, there is no phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place. The order in which applications are received counts from the outset.
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_no_list#:#Rejection
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_no_list_info#:#The waiting list is only used for applications for acceptance to the course. If no more places are available, applications are rejected.
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_short#:#First come, first served
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_waiting#:#Manual allocation of places on waiting list
common#:#sub_fair_inactive_waiting_info#:#Places that subsequently become free have to be filled manually using the participant management function.
common#:#sub_fair_no_list#:#Automatic allocation of places and then rejection
common#:#sub_fair_no_list_info#:#The waiting list is only filled during the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place, and the places then allocated automatically. If no more places are available after that, all further applications are rejected.
common#:#sub_fair_not_changeable#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place cannot be shortened, as this would affect existing registrations.
common#:#sub_fair_not_on_list#:#Not on the list
common#:#sub_fair_position_with_other#:#%s (with 1 where all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place)
common#:#sub_fair_position_with_others#:#%s (with %s where all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place)
common#:#sub_fair_subscribe_label#:#Register for allocation of places
common#:#sub_fair_subscribe_message#:#Up until %s all applications are collected with all applicants having equal chances of obtaining a place, and then the places are assigned by drawing lots.
common#:#sub_fair_subscription_min_minutes#:#The time available for registering must last at least %s minutes.
common#:#sub_fair_time_before#:#before %s
common#:#sub_fair_to_act_end#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been restricted until availability ends.
common#:#sub_fair_to_act_start_min#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been restricted to the minimum time period after availability begins.
common#:#sub_fair_to_sub_end#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been restricted to the end of the registration period.
common#:#sub_fair_to_sub_start_min#:#The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place has been set at the minimum time period after registration begins.
common#:#sub_fair_wait_pos_header#:#Pos.
common#:#sub_fair_waiting#:#Manual allocation of places and assignment of places on waiting list
common#:#sub_fair_waiting_info#:#After the phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place, free places have to be assigned manually using the participant management function. Only select these settings if acceptance depends on additional criteria.
common#:#sub_fill_free_places#:#Fill free places
common#:#sub_fill_free_places_question#:#Would you like to fill free places from the waiting list?
common#:#sub_mail_autofill_requests_body#:#The free places are filled from the waiting list. However, some places are kept free for applications for acceptance to the course, and you are required to make a decision about them.
