fau#:#fau_sub_accept_all_groups#:#The applications for acceptance are accepted in the course and all included parallel groups.
fau#:#fau_sub_after_date#:#The entry procedure for courses in winter semester 2022/23 can be entered from July 26.
fau#:#fau_sub_combi_disabled#:#A group selection must be made for this course. If you would like to use the combined registration function, set it up outside of the course and add all parallel groups to the course.
fau#:#fau_sub_direct_possible#:#Direct acceptance possible
fau#:#fau_sub_group_by_course_group_settings#:#Participants join this parallel group after passing a selection process for joining the course. You cannot select your own acceptance procedure for the group but you can limit the number of participants. That is taken into consideration when students register for courses.
fau#:#fau_sub_group_by_course_info#:#This course includes parallel groups from a teaching unit. They are provided for selection on the registration page for the course. Students can only join one of these groups directly, but they can place their names on the waiting list several times.
fau#:#fau_sub_group_by_course_limit_info#:#The maximum number of participants is entered separately for each parallel group for this course. The phase during which all applicants have equal chances of obtaining a place and waiting list options are entered in the course and are required when students select groups with a limited number of participants. It does not apply to groups with no restrictions on places.
fau#:#fau_sub_group_by_course_list_info#:#About joining courses
fau#:#fau_sub_refuse_all_groups#:#The applications for acceptance are rejected for the course and all included parallel groups.
fau#:#fau_sub_select_groups#:#Group selection
fau#:#fau_sub_select_groups_info#:#Please select one or more parallel groups from this teaching unit. If possible, you will be accepted directly into one of them, otherwise you will be placed on the waiting list for all selected groups.
fau#:#fau_sub_select_module_info#:#Choose the module or area for which you would like to attend this teaching unit. This information is important and later appears on your final academic record.
fau#:#fau_sub_select_module_info2#:#The list contains all modules/areas that are assigned to your courses of study. A check mark (✓) means that the requirements of the module/area are fulfilled. A cross (✗) means that they are not fulfilled. You can only select such entries if there is no selectable alternative. Then, with the acceptance of your registration request, it is decided that the prerequisites can be ignored.###
